# Branding

This lab’s brand is **Agentic Engineering** (site title: **Agentic Engineering Lab**).

## Do

- Use “Agentic Engineering” / “Agentic Engineering Lab” when a product name is needed
- Describe the domain plainly: projects, agents, runs, approvals, fixtures, remote functions
- Keep copy open-ended — the theme is a light backdrop for teaching SvelteKit patterns

## Don’t

- Never use “Control Plane”, “control plane”, or “control-plane” in branding, titles, docs, UI copy, package metadata, or comments
- Don’t lean on marketing jargon (“orchestration platform”, “AI Eng control plane”, etc.)
- Don’t cram “agentic” into every sentence, fixture name, or lesson scenario

## Examples

```text
❌ Control Plane Lab
✅ Agentic Engineering Lab

❌ An operator opens the control plane…
✅ An operator needs the current project list…

❌ themed as an AI Eng control plane
✅ teaching lab with agentic engineering entities (projects, agents, runs)
```
